WEBVTT

00:35.500 --> 00:38.340
Tvnnouncer:
From time life music,
comes a one-of-a kind

00:38.408 --> 00:41.447
Rat pack collection,
"their most bigoted songs."

00:41.516 --> 00:43.755
All your favorite,
once acceptable hits like

00:43.987 --> 00:45.223
"drunk old injun."

00:47.030 --> 00:50.004
♪ the drunk old injun's
squattin' in his teepee ♪

00:50.072 --> 00:52.677
♪ fire water keepin' him warm. ♪

00:52.744 --> 00:54.381
Announcer:
"jewish nose"

00:54.449 --> 00:57.992
♪ she's got a big, beautiful
jewish nose ♪

00:58.060 --> 01:01.435
♪ and it's there two minutes
early wherever she goes. ♪

01:01.502 --> 01:04.677
Announcer:
Dean martin singing
"chinaman's chance."

01:04.745 --> 01:08.153
♪ and mr. Chinaman say,
in his chinaman way ♪

01:08.221 --> 01:11.697
♪ a ding-a-ling, a ching-a-chong
a ching-a-chong choo. ♪

01:11.765 --> 01:14.940
Announcer:
"pew, stinky frenchman."

01:15.008 --> 01:18.015
♪ paris is lovely and nice
sure is nice ♪

01:18.082 --> 01:21.391
♪ and marseilles is charming
with champagne on ice ♪

01:21.458 --> 01:24.867
♪ but you, stinky frenchman,
haven't a clue ♪

01:24.936 --> 01:28.344
♪ pew, stinky frenchman,
frog you. ♪

01:28.412 --> 01:29.747
"hey there, fruity."

01:31.219 --> 01:32.722
♪ hey there, fruity ♪

01:32.790 --> 01:34.493
♪ you can do my hair ♪

01:34.562 --> 01:36.031
♪ hey there, fruity ♪

01:36.099 --> 01:37.937
♪ don't touch me down there ♪

01:38.005 --> 01:39.575
♪ hey there, fruity ♪

01:39.643 --> 01:43.051
♪ you're gay and I
don't approve. ♪

01:43.119 --> 01:45.057
Announcer:
And many more!

01:46.696 --> 01:48.265
You know, I'm sick of
looking at that.

01:48.334 --> 01:49.837
What?
That empty space.

01:49.904 --> 01:52.176
It just reminds me that
cleveland's not here anymore.

01:52.244 --> 01:53.814
Yeah, it's just not
the same without him.

01:53.882 --> 01:55.019
I sure wish he...

01:55.086 --> 01:56.656
Hey, guys, look!

01:57.859 --> 01:58.928
It's him!

01:58.996 --> 02:00.332
Hey, cleveland!

02:00.401 --> 02:02.772
Why didn't you tell us
you were back, buddy?

02:02.839 --> 02:04.177
Oh, it's a lamp.

02:05.515 --> 02:08.456
You know, guys,
I've been thinkin'.

02:08.524 --> 02:10.594
We need a new fourth
guy for our group.

02:10.662 --> 02:11.732
We're a man short.

02:11.800 --> 02:13.336
Like stadler
without waldorf.

02:13.404 --> 02:14.739
(laughing)

02:14.807 --> 02:16.410
You know, without the other guy
yappin' in my ear,

02:16.478 --> 02:17.780
These guys aren't half bad.

02:21.861 --> 02:24.300
Now I know you're interested
in being the fourth guy

02:24.367 --> 02:26.572
In our entourage,
kevin connolly, but don't you

02:26.639 --> 02:28.812
Think you're a little small?
Listen, I tell you what.

02:28.880 --> 02:31.285
You can be in our group
if I can have some
of your cereal.

02:31.353 --> 02:33.926
Oh, no! They're after
me kevin connolly charms!

02:40.277 --> 02:41.715
How's your friend
search going?

02:41.782 --> 02:43.820
(sighs) not great, lois.
What friend search?

02:43.889 --> 02:44.823
Oh, we're just trying to find

02:44.891 --> 02:45.826
A friend to replace cleveland.

02:45.895 --> 02:46.829
We've been meeting people

02:46.897 --> 02:48.199
For the past three days.

02:48.267 --> 02:49.770
Well, you don't
need to look for
somebody new.

02:49.838 --> 02:51.675
I'll hang out
with you guys.
Yeah, you know,

02:51.744 --> 02:53.246
I don't think that's
gonna work out, brian,

02:53.314 --> 02:54.416
'cause of the whole
quagmire thing.

02:54.484 --> 02:55.820
What quagmire thing?

02:55.889 --> 02:57.324
Oh, you know, just
that he hates you.

02:57.392 --> 02:59.364
Quagmire hates me?
Hates you.

02:59.431 --> 03:01.937
I-I don't get it.
Why, why wouldn't
quagmire like me?

03:02.004 --> 03:03.576
Because he thinks
you're annoying.

03:03.642 --> 03:05.747
Like people who never
shut up about their kids.

03:05.815 --> 03:08.489
He, he would have
been four today.

03:08.557 --> 03:10.728
I-I still don't
understand.

03:10.796 --> 03:13.236
How do you drown
in an inch of water?

03:13.303 --> 03:15.307
(sobbing)
well...

03:15.375 --> 03:18.383
I guess I don't
have a new sweater
and a haircut.

03:22.696 --> 03:23.965
(sighs):
Who would've thought

03:24.033 --> 03:25.536
It would be this hard
to replace cleveland?

03:25.604 --> 03:27.007
You know, guys,
we've kind of been

03:27.074 --> 03:28.412
Ignoring the obvious here.

03:28.480 --> 03:30.016
I mean, if you really
break it down,

03:30.084 --> 03:31.788
What we need is a black guy.

03:31.856 --> 03:33.893
Yeah, that was the best thing
about cleveland.

03:33.961 --> 03:36.033
Oh, by far.
I sure do miss him.

03:36.100 --> 03:38.071
Peter's right.
We gotta find another black guy.

03:38.139 --> 03:39.241
Yeah, 'cause
otherwise we're just

03:39.310 --> 03:40.679
A bunch of boring
white guys.

03:40.746 --> 03:42.517
Like a london
gentlemen's club.

03:42.584 --> 03:45.225
(clears throat)

03:45.293 --> 03:47.464
(clears throat)

03:47.532 --> 03:48.701
(clears throat)

03:48.768 --> 03:49.937
(clears throat)

03:50.005 --> 03:51.274
(clears throat)

03:51.342 --> 03:53.146
(clears throat)

03:53.214 --> 03:55.051
(clears throat)

03:55.120 --> 03:56.689
(clears throat)

03:56.757 --> 03:58.595
(clears throat)

03:58.662 --> 03:59.998
(clears throat louder)

04:00.066 --> 04:01.470
(clears throat)

04:01.537 --> 04:03.509
(clears throat loudly)

04:03.577 --> 04:04.812
(clears throat
even louder)

04:04.880 --> 04:06.384
(clears throat
loudly)

04:06.451 --> 04:08.590
(clears throat
even louder)

04:08.657 --> 04:10.596
(clears throat
loudly)

04:10.663 --> 04:12.198
(clears throat
loudly)

04:12.267 --> 04:15.877
(angrily clears throat)

04:15.944 --> 04:19.286
(annoyingly
clears throat)

04:19.355 --> 04:21.392
(clears throat
noisily)

04:21.460 --> 04:22.562
(clears throat)

04:22.630 --> 04:24.099
(clears throat)

04:24.167 --> 04:26.807
(clears throat quietly)

04:26.875 --> 04:28.411
(clears throat
a bit softer)

04:28.479 --> 04:29.916
(clears throat
even softer)

04:29.983 --> 04:31.386
(clears throat softly)

04:31.455 --> 04:32.657
(clears throat
briefly)

04:32.725 --> 04:35.164
(clears throat
softly)

04:35.232 --> 04:37.336
(clears throat
very quietly)

04:37.404 --> 04:40.144
Hey, you guys want to
enter the darts tournament?

04:40.213 --> 04:42.182
First prize is free
drinks all night.

04:42.251 --> 04:44.423
Oh, we'd love to,
horace, but there's
only three of us.

04:44.491 --> 04:46.328
Man:
Did I hear some sorry ass fools

04:46.395 --> 04:48.267
In need of a motherlovin'
fourth?

04:53.382 --> 04:55.553
I'll join
your darts game.

04:55.622 --> 04:56.858
How do we know
you're any good?

05:01.270 --> 05:04.445
Gentlemen,
we got us a black man.

05:05.950 --> 05:07.821
(all laughing)

05:09.126 --> 05:11.900
Oh, boy, what
a fantastic evening.

05:11.968 --> 05:14.706
Jerome, you are a wonderful
addition to our group.

05:14.774 --> 05:16.145
Hey, thanks, peter.

05:16.212 --> 05:17.682
I like you guys, too.

05:17.750 --> 05:20.256
What do you say we hit
another bar, keep it goin'?

05:20.325 --> 05:23.096
I can't. There's a girl
tied up in my basement
who needs some food.

05:23.165 --> 05:25.738
That's funny.
You funny, pointy man.

05:25.806 --> 05:27.877
Yeah, I...
I joke around a lot.

05:33.092 --> 05:34.396
Thanks for the lift
home, jerome.

05:34.464 --> 05:35.833
Hey, if you got
time to come in,

05:35.900 --> 05:37.202
I'd love for you
to meet my wife.

05:37.269 --> 05:39.309
I got time for
whatever I want, fool.

05:39.377 --> 05:42.050
My watch don't tell
time, I tell it.

05:42.117 --> 05:45.292
Wow, you're cooler than
a york peppermint pattie.

05:45.360 --> 05:47.398
When I bite
into a york peppermint pattie,

05:47.465 --> 05:49.438
I get the sensation...

05:49.506 --> 05:52.914
Of being on a frozen
mountaintop!

05:52.981 --> 05:55.854
<i>It has been two months
since I made the tragic choice</i>

05:55.922 --> 05:57.994
<i>To bite
into a york peppermint pattie,</i>

05:58.062 --> 05:59.732
<i>And still I have made
no progress</i>

05:59.800 --> 06:01.538
<i>Finding my way
out of the mountains.</i>

06:01.605 --> 06:03.610
<i>The only food I have
is the rest of this</i>

06:03.678 --> 06:05.949
<i>York peppermint pattie,
which unfortunately,</i>

06:06.017 --> 06:08.423
<i>Keeps bringing me back
to the top of the mountain.</i>

06:08.491 --> 06:11.833
<i>If anyone finds this,
tell my family I love them.</i>

06:11.900 --> 06:14.172
...Of being on a frozen
mountaintop!

06:18.319 --> 06:20.324
Hey, lois. I'd like you
to meet our new friend...

06:20.391 --> 06:21.325
Jerome?

06:21.392 --> 06:22.763
Loose lois?

06:22.831 --> 06:24.834
Wha... You guys
know each other?

06:24.903 --> 06:26.273
Know each other?

06:26.340 --> 06:28.680
Peter, jerome is an
old boyfriend of mine.

06:28.748 --> 06:30.551
What?!
(stewie yawning)

06:30.619 --> 06:32.423
Sorry, I was out of it.
Wait, are we being robbed?

06:37.121 --> 06:39.660
Peter, I know I told
you about jerome.

06:39.727 --> 06:41.497
Lois, I would've remembered
if you told me that.

06:41.566 --> 06:43.003
I told you, peter.

06:43.070 --> 06:45.075
I remember exactly
what we were doing.

06:45.142 --> 06:47.014
(both laughing)

06:49.053 --> 06:50.791
I slept with a black guy.

06:50.859 --> 06:53.699
I hope this doesn't make
you feel awkward, my man.

06:53.767 --> 06:55.604
It was a long time ago.

06:55.672 --> 06:57.142
Hey, that's
a beautiful baby.

06:57.209 --> 06:58.379
Mind if I hold him?

06:58.446 --> 07:00.050
Go right ahead.

07:00.118 --> 07:01.688
Hey there, lil' fella.

07:01.756 --> 07:02.992
What's that around
your neck?

07:03.059 --> 07:05.432
Well, I say, it's
a little black jesus.

07:05.500 --> 07:07.605
♪ black jesus. ♪

07:07.672 --> 07:10.346
I rode into town
on an ass.

07:10.414 --> 07:12.250
Your mama's ass.

07:12.317 --> 07:15.092
♪ black jesus. ♪

07:15.160 --> 07:17.031
It was really good
to see you, lois.

07:17.099 --> 07:19.270
We should grab a coffee
or something and catch up.

07:19.338 --> 07:21.109
That would be great.

07:21.177 --> 07:23.081
It was really nice
to see you, too.

07:23.148 --> 07:24.384
Well, it's gettin'
late, jerome.

07:24.453 --> 07:26.122
I'm sure you got stuff to do.

07:26.192 --> 07:28.128
Yeah, I gotta go down
to the gas station

07:28.196 --> 07:30.000
And buy a framed
painting of a tiger.

07:30.068 --> 07:32.339
Catch y'all later.

07:32.407 --> 07:34.580
You're not really gonna
hang out with him, lois, are ya?

07:34.648 --> 07:36.352
We're just friends, peter.

07:36.419 --> 07:37.855
Don't tell me
you're jealous?

07:37.923 --> 07:41.197
Well, you datin' that guy?
It's just a lot to take in.

07:41.266 --> 07:43.102
(laughs):
Oh, you're tellin' me.

07:43.171 --> 07:45.276
Oh, come on! Those kinds
of jokes aren't helpin'.

07:45.344 --> 07:46.947
Well, what do you
want me to say?

07:47.015 --> 07:48.485
You're bein' silly.

07:48.553 --> 07:51.661
I mean, jerome and I
dated over 12 inches ago.

07:51.729 --> 07:53.633
(laughs):
I said inches!

07:53.700 --> 07:55.738
What did I just say?!
I'm sorry.

07:55.805 --> 07:58.078
I'm sorry. Okay,
look, just relax.

07:58.145 --> 08:00.452
You're my husband
and I love you,

08:00.520 --> 08:02.090
So just put jerome
out of your head.

08:03.394 --> 08:05.500
Get him out of my life
is more like it.

08:08.341 --> 08:10.914
Brian, I just found
out chris farley died.

08:10.982 --> 08:12.752
Yeah, that happened
like 12 years ago.

08:12.820 --> 08:14.557
<i>But I just watched
tommy boy yesterday.</i>

08:14.626 --> 08:16.363
He was right there.
Yeah, that's a movie.

08:16.431 --> 08:18.769
It's shot beforehand.
It's not happening right now.

08:18.837 --> 08:21.476
Really? But I thought
my knocking on the tv glass

08:21.544 --> 08:23.917
Distracted him,
and that's what made
him fall down that hill.

08:23.985 --> 08:25.990
(laughing):
Oh, oh, seeing him
fall down that hill

08:26.057 --> 08:27.561
Put me in a good humor!

08:27.629 --> 08:28.797
Stewie, get lost.

08:28.865 --> 08:30.469
What are you doing
just standing out here?

08:30.536 --> 08:32.339
I'm waiting for quagmire
to get his mail.

08:32.407 --> 08:33.977
I'm gonna conveniently
stroll by

08:34.045 --> 08:35.483
And strike up a
conversation with him,

08:35.550 --> 08:37.154
And maybe find out
why he hates me.

08:37.222 --> 08:38.792
Oh, I'm sure it's just
a misunderstanding.

08:38.860 --> 08:40.296
You'll smooth it over.

08:43.472 --> 08:45.511
Hey, quagmire,
what a coincidence.

08:45.578 --> 08:47.448
You and me just runnin'
into each other.

08:47.516 --> 08:48.787
How, how ya doin'?
Fine.

08:51.695 --> 08:53.399
Oh, takin' a break, huh?

08:53.467 --> 08:55.036
She's a hot piece of ass.

08:55.105 --> 08:56.975
And from the looks of it,
she likes it rough.

08:57.043 --> 08:58.346
That's my sister, brian.

08:58.414 --> 09:00.352
Her boyfriend has been
beating her mercilessly.

09:00.419 --> 09:02.691
The last thing she'd
want right now is to
be objectified.

09:02.759 --> 09:04.964
Oh, god.
I'm, I'm really sorry.

09:05.032 --> 09:07.003
I got a deaf brother,
you want to make fun
of him, too?

09:08.175 --> 09:09.175
(door closes)

09:09.244 --> 09:10.146
(brakes screeching)

09:13.322 --> 09:14.759
Man:
Where is she?
Quagmire:
She's not here.

09:14.826 --> 09:15.962
Harriet:
Get out, jeff!

09:16.029 --> 09:17.666
Just get out of here!

09:17.734 --> 09:19.638
Oh, I'll get out
when I'm finished.

09:19.707 --> 09:21.042
(punch landing,
glass shattering)
harriet: No! Ow!

09:21.110 --> 09:23.149
You feel good about your sex
joke earlier, brian?

09:23.215 --> 09:25.221
He's savagely beating her again.
You hear that?

09:25.289 --> 09:26.458
Yeah, I'm not deaf.

09:26.526 --> 09:27.995
Oh, oh, what, like my brother?

09:28.063 --> 09:29.599
Boy, you have no class!

09:29.668 --> 09:31.405
Man:
Yeah, that's the
guy's brother, man!

09:31.473 --> 09:32.942
Harriet:
Yeah!
Shut up, bitch!
(fist smacking)

09:36.921 --> 09:38.792
Hey, you know
what they say.

09:38.861 --> 09:41.400
See a broad,
to get that booty, yak 'em.

09:41.468 --> 09:43.772
Quagmire & jerome:
Leg her down and
smack 'em yak 'em!

09:43.840 --> 09:45.579
(laughs)
cold got to be.

09:45.646 --> 09:47.684
(both laughing)

09:47.751 --> 09:49.422
Golly!
If you'll excuse me,

09:49.490 --> 09:51.227
I'm gonna order me
some cheap cognac

09:51.294 --> 09:53.633
And put it
in a fancy glass.

09:53.701 --> 09:55.036
Boy, jerome
is the greatest.

09:55.104 --> 09:56.174
We really lucked out.

09:56.242 --> 09:57.344
I don't know, you guys.

09:57.410 --> 09:58.847
I'm not so sure
about jerome.

09:58.916 --> 10:00.785
I mean, how do we know
we can really trust him?

10:00.853 --> 10:03.260
What are you talking about,
peter? Jerome's awesome.

10:03.327 --> 10:05.132
Yeah, why the hell wouldn't
we be able to trust him?

10:05.200 --> 10:06.702
All right, you guys
want the truth?

10:06.770 --> 10:09.411
Before me and lois were married,
our new friend

10:09.479 --> 10:11.417
Used to slip her
the old pringles can.

10:11.485 --> 10:14.324
Well, so what, peter.
That was 20 years ago.

10:14.392 --> 10:15.562
That doesn't matter!

10:15.629 --> 10:17.400
Look, peter,
jerome's the coolest guy

10:17.466 --> 10:18.904
We've met since
cleveland left.

10:18.972 --> 10:21.209
Yeah, don't do anything
to ruin this, peter.

10:21.278 --> 10:23.250
You know, the way you
ruined my parrot.

10:23.317 --> 10:24.854
I just bought
it yesterday.

10:24.922 --> 10:26.324
Isn't it beautiful?

10:26.392 --> 10:28.396
Cripple, cripple, cripple,
cripple, cripple, cripple,

10:28.464 --> 10:29.802
Cripple, cripple,
cripple, cripple.

10:29.869 --> 10:31.104
Cripple!
Damn it!

10:35.517 --> 10:37.021
That son of a bitch.

10:37.089 --> 10:38.726
Thinks he can sleep
with my wife!

10:38.793 --> 10:40.129
Not on my watch.

10:42.838 --> 10:44.975
Alex keaton (on tv):
Listen, I don't care that
you're dating mallory.

10:45.043 --> 10:46.849
Nobody in this family
likes you, nick.

10:46.916 --> 10:49.622
You just stand your ground,
garbage sculpture man.

10:49.690 --> 10:51.227
They'll come to respect you.

10:51.294 --> 10:52.597
You bastard.

10:52.665 --> 10:54.069
Nick was no good for her

10:54.137 --> 10:55.939
And it broke
skippy handleman's heart!

11:05.868 --> 11:08.542
Dear god and black jesus!

11:15.996 --> 11:16.998
Jerome?

11:17.066 --> 11:18.469
What, uh...

11:18.536 --> 11:20.140
What-- what the hell
are you doing here?

11:20.208 --> 11:22.614
Oh, peter, something
terrible has happened.

11:22.682 --> 11:24.888
Somebody burned down
jerome's house last night.

11:24.956 --> 11:27.763
This whacked-out world.

11:27.830 --> 11:29.768
It just makes you want
to grab your nephew

11:29.836 --> 11:32.241
And get in a van and shoot
people in the d.C. Area.

11:32.308 --> 11:34.816
Yeah, well, when I find
the guy who did it,

11:34.884 --> 11:37.991
I'm gonna rip his arms off and
do his wife in front of him.

11:38.058 --> 11:39.695
And no one would blame you.

11:39.763 --> 11:41.166
But, meanwhile, jerome,

11:41.234 --> 11:42.971
You are more than
welcome to stay with us.

11:43.039 --> 11:44.108
What?

11:44.176 --> 11:45.746
Oh, well, thank
you, lois.

11:45.814 --> 11:48.954
Man, I'm so lucky to have real
friends like you and peter.

11:49.023 --> 11:50.425
Well, I guess
you can stay here.

11:50.493 --> 11:51.728
But I'll tell you
one thing...

11:51.796 --> 11:53.267
Oh, hang on a second.

11:53.335 --> 11:55.104
What is that?

11:55.172 --> 11:57.378
I don't know, it's trying
to do something.

11:57.446 --> 11:58.949
Oh...

11:59.017 --> 12:01.857
Well, well, I guess we're
just gonna have to wait.

12:06.732 --> 12:09.739
So how long is jerome
gonna be staying with us, dad?

12:09.807 --> 12:12.346
I don't know, chris,
but the sooner he's out
of here, the better.

12:12.415 --> 12:14.519
I don't trust him around
lois for a second.

12:14.587 --> 12:17.661
Lois:
Oh, god, jerome,
that is so good.

12:17.728 --> 12:20.403
Oh, yeah,
it's so hot and moist.

12:22.709 --> 12:25.248
Mmm, these scones are
delicious.

12:25.317 --> 12:27.556
You are quite the little baker,
jerome.

12:27.623 --> 12:28.692
Oh, thank god.

12:28.759 --> 12:30.262
What's going on in here?!

12:30.331 --> 12:31.601
Relax, mr. Furley.

12:31.668 --> 12:33.239
I thought what you
thought, but it's okay.

12:33.306 --> 12:35.678
Well, it sounded like...
I know, I know, but it's fine.

12:35.747 --> 12:37.350
Go back to being dead.

12:37.418 --> 12:38.853
Peter, is everything
all right?

12:38.921 --> 12:40.591
Yeah. Yeah, lois.
Everything's fine.

12:40.659 --> 12:42.865
You guys, uh, having
a little breakfast?

12:42.933 --> 12:45.137
Yes, and jerome
made scones.

12:45.205 --> 12:47.913
Would you like one?
Oh, they're delicious.

12:47.980 --> 12:50.285
I thought maybe later
today, we could all...

12:50.353 --> 12:52.792
(choking)

12:52.861 --> 12:54.933
Oh, my god!
Mom's choking!

12:55.000 --> 12:56.803
Out of the way.
I'm an emt.

13:01.384 --> 13:03.055
Her airway's jammed.

13:03.122 --> 13:04.291
Come on, now.
Just like that.

13:04.358 --> 13:05.796
(both grunting)

13:05.863 --> 13:07.666
I need some
gravitational help.

13:09.505 --> 13:11.713
Oh, no, her clothes
are constricting!

13:11.780 --> 13:13.583
As are mine!

13:13.651 --> 13:15.522
(breathing heavily)

13:18.432 --> 13:19.600
(coughs)

13:19.668 --> 13:21.004
Oh, my god!

13:21.071 --> 13:23.143
Oh! Thank you, jerome!

13:23.212 --> 13:24.950
You saved my life!

13:25.018 --> 13:27.656
"um, I'll have
what she's having,"

13:27.723 --> 13:29.928
Says the funniest person
in the room.

13:34.843 --> 13:36.715
Hey, what are you getting
all dressed up for?

13:36.783 --> 13:38.553
I'm treating quagmire
to a night out.

13:38.621 --> 13:39.923
Really? I thought
he hated you.

13:39.992 --> 13:41.227
How'd you
convince him to go?

13:41.295 --> 13:43.032
I tricked him.
Sent him a phony card.

13:43.100 --> 13:45.271
He thinks he's going
on a date with an
old girlfriend.

13:45.339 --> 13:47.211
But instead,
you're going to show up.

13:47.279 --> 13:48.816
You got it.
Yikes.

13:48.883 --> 13:50.520
That's a recipe
for disappointment.

13:50.588 --> 13:52.158
Like walking
a floral arrangement

13:52.226 --> 13:53.594
Through an office
full of fat women.

13:55.167 --> 13:56.704
Is there
a miss...
(excited gasping)

13:56.772 --> 13:58.274
...Es.
(all sighing)

14:02.855 --> 14:05.461
Brian?
Where's cheryl tiegs?

14:05.529 --> 14:07.299
Well, she's not coming.

14:07.367 --> 14:09.874
I wrote you that,
because I knew you'd
never come if it was me.

14:09.941 --> 14:12.380
But I planned a big
night and we're gonna
have a great time.

14:12.448 --> 14:14.988
Brian, cheryl was the one
that got away.

14:15.056 --> 14:17.026
She was the great love
of my life.

14:17.095 --> 14:18.799
I thought this was my chance

14:18.866 --> 14:20.871
To finally achieve
some real happiness.

14:20.939 --> 14:23.412
Ever since she left,
I've been chasing girls

14:23.480 --> 14:25.584
To fill the hole she made
when she walked out.

14:25.652 --> 14:27.422
And now I'm forever lost.

14:27.490 --> 14:29.494
Well, I bet a thick,
juicy steak

14:29.563 --> 14:31.033
Could help fill
that hole, huh?

14:31.099 --> 14:32.972
(sobbing)

14:34.911 --> 14:37.082
Aw, come on,
it'll be great.

14:37.151 --> 14:39.791
Listen, glenn,
I-I want us to be friends.

14:39.859 --> 14:41.864
I think we could be
an even better team

14:41.930 --> 14:44.637
Than lewis and clark
and the guy who likes
to rip up maps.

14:44.805 --> 14:47.713
All right,
the northwest passage.E.

14:47.779 --> 14:49.784
Hey, can I see that?

14:51.256 --> 14:52.859
Damn it! You ass!

14:52.927 --> 14:54.999
Easy, clark.
I hate that guy!

14:55.068 --> 14:56.235
It's been a long trip.

14:56.304 --> 14:57.974
You're tired.
No! I hate him!

14:58.042 --> 15:00.281
Look, you're angry,
you're dehydrated.

15:00.348 --> 15:02.019
Just have some water
from the canteen

15:02.086 --> 15:04.326
And you'll feel better.
Okay.

15:04.394 --> 15:06.698
I just totally drowned
this ant hill.

15:06.767 --> 15:13.283
Hey, when are we
going to get there?

15:13.351 --> 15:16.526
Oh, and this is peter
and I at our wedding.

15:16.593 --> 15:18.097
Aw, you look beautiful.

15:18.165 --> 15:19.902
And he's a handsome
fella, ain't he?

15:19.970 --> 15:21.808
Well, I am ready
for my evening.

15:21.875 --> 15:23.278
Oh, my god, peter!

15:23.346 --> 15:25.551
What the hell?!
Peter, what are you doing?

15:25.618 --> 15:27.924
Oh, surely, jerome,
you don't want to stay
in the same house

15:27.992 --> 15:30.030
As a ghost who carries
a torch around.

15:30.099 --> 15:32.537
Ooh, fire ghost!

15:32.606 --> 15:34.310
Ooh! Ya scared yet?

15:34.378 --> 15:35.948
Didn't know this place
was haunted, did ya?

15:36.016 --> 15:37.450
Peter, take that
thing off!

15:37.518 --> 15:38.921
Hey, what the hell's
going on?

15:38.989 --> 15:40.226
I'll tell you
what's going on.

15:40.293 --> 15:42.030
I have had about
enough of you, jerome.

15:42.097 --> 15:44.337
I know you want my wife,
but you can't have her!

15:44.406 --> 15:46.410
You are no longer
welcome in my house!

15:46.477 --> 15:48.114
Whatchu talkin' 'bout, peter?
(laughs)

15:48.182 --> 15:49.684
But you can't have
sex with lois!

15:49.753 --> 15:51.490
Now, I want you out
of here right now!

15:51.558 --> 15:53.930
I can't believe this.

15:53.998 --> 15:56.169
I thought I found
a true friend in you.

15:56.236 --> 15:59.814
I'd never do anything to hurt
you or your family.

15:59.881 --> 16:02.019
Man, you're breaking my heart.

16:02.087 --> 16:03.423
Jerome, wait.

16:03.492 --> 16:05.229
He doesn't know what
he's talking about.

16:05.297 --> 16:06.800
I'm sorry, lois.

16:06.868 --> 16:09.139
I think it would be
better if I left.

16:09.207 --> 16:12.281
Peter, I'm sorry
if I caused you any trouble.

16:12.349 --> 16:15.190
I won't be bothering
you again.

16:17.731 --> 16:21.006
Wow, what just happened
was kind of sad.

16:21.074 --> 16:25.619
<i>(hums family guy theme morosely)</i>

16:35.648 --> 16:38.187
So... Whose leg
do you have to hump

16:38.254 --> 16:39.723
To get a dry martini
around here?

16:39.792 --> 16:41.931
(chuckles)
hmm.

16:41.998 --> 16:44.003
God, look at the size
of these steak knives.

16:44.071 --> 16:46.275
Wha-what are they serving us?
Tyrannosaurus rex?

16:46.343 --> 16:49.117
Not likely.

16:49.185 --> 16:53.195
Hey, what if I just drank
this whole bottle of ketchup?

16:53.263 --> 16:55.067
Can you imagine?
You dare me?

16:55.134 --> 16:56.738
Kind of ruins it
for the next person

16:56.806 --> 16:58.810
Who might want
some ketchup.

16:58.877 --> 17:00.481
So, how's
the flying business?

17:00.549 --> 17:03.156
Not so great.
The economy's sort
of taken its toll,

17:03.224 --> 17:05.763
Lot of salary cuts,
lot of layoffs.
Yeah?

17:05.831 --> 17:07.166
That's pretty much it.

17:07.234 --> 17:09.607
I mean, you want to learn
more, read the papers,

17:09.675 --> 17:11.113
Go on the internet,
I-I don't know.

17:11.180 --> 17:12.548
Boy, that's got to be
an interesting job.

17:12.616 --> 17:14.253
I'll bet you got--
how do those things work?

17:14.321 --> 17:16.059
What? Planes?

17:16.127 --> 17:18.465
How does a plane work?
Yeah.

17:18.533 --> 17:21.273
You want me to sit here
and explain to you
how a plane works?

17:21.341 --> 17:22.844
I don't know. Yeah.

17:22.912 --> 17:24.148
You want to maybe just go?

17:24.215 --> 17:26.187
Quagmire, come on,
I'm really trying hard here.

17:26.255 --> 17:27.590
Who asked you to try hard?

17:27.658 --> 17:29.662
Nobody, but all--
I'm trying to establish

17:29.730 --> 17:30.966
A friendship with you.

17:31.034 --> 17:32.971
All I've done is try
to be nice to you,

17:33.039 --> 17:35.512
And you still don't like me.
How can you not like me?

17:35.580 --> 17:37.618
Okay. I'll tell you.

17:37.686 --> 17:39.891
You are the worst person I know.

17:39.959 --> 17:41.663
You constantly hit on your
best friend's wife.

17:41.732 --> 17:43.435
The man pays for your food
and rescued you

17:43.503 --> 17:45.341
From certain death,
and this is how you repay him?

17:45.409 --> 17:48.281
And to add insult to injury,
you defecate all over his yard.

17:48.349 --> 17:50.554
And you're such a sponge.
You pay for nothing.

17:50.622 --> 17:52.127
You always say,
"oh, I'll get you later."

17:52.193 --> 17:53.429
But later never comes.

17:53.497 --> 17:55.302
And what really bothers me,
is you pretend

17:55.370 --> 17:57.641
You're this deep guy who loves
women for their souls

17:57.709 --> 17:59.246
When all you do is date bimbos.

17:59.313 --> 18:01.050
Yeah, I date women
for their bodies,

18:01.119 --> 18:02.488
But at least
I'm honest about it.

18:02.556 --> 18:04.293
<i>I don't buy them a copy
of catcher in the rye</i>

18:04.361 --> 18:06.800
And then lecture them with some
seventh grade interpretation

18:06.867 --> 18:09.307
Of how holden caulfield
is some profound, intellectual.

18:09.375 --> 18:11.446
He wasn't.
He was a spoiled brat.

18:11.513 --> 18:13.418
And that's why you like him
so much-- he's you.

18:13.486 --> 18:14.755
God, you're pretentious!

18:14.823 --> 18:16.561
And you delude yourself
by thinking you're some

18:16.628 --> 18:17.865
Great writer,
even though you're terrible.

18:17.933 --> 18:19.235
You know, I should have known
cheryl tiegs

18:19.303 --> 18:20.772
Didn't write me that note.

18:20.841 --> 18:22.979
She would have known there's no
"a" in the word "definite."

18:23.046 --> 18:24.683
And I think
what I hate most about you

18:24.750 --> 18:26.689
Is your textbook liberal agenda,
how we should

18:26.756 --> 18:28.293
"legalize pot, man,"

18:28.361 --> 18:30.232
How big business
is crushing the underclass,

18:30.300 --> 18:32.438
How homelessness is the biggest
tragedy in america.

18:32.506 --> 18:33.775
Well, what have you done
to help?

18:33.843 --> 18:35.380
I work down at the soup kitchen,
brian.

18:35.448 --> 18:36.817
Never seen you down there.

18:36.885 --> 18:38.355
You want to help?
Grab a ladle!

18:38.422 --> 18:41.530
And, by the way, driving a prius
doesn't make you jesus christ.

18:41.598 --> 18:43.201
Oh, wait, you don't believe
in jesus christ,

18:43.270 --> 18:44.640
Or any religion for that matter,

18:44.706 --> 18:46.176
Because "religion is
for idiots."

18:46.244 --> 18:48.181
Well, who the hell are you
to talk down to anyone?

18:48.250 --> 18:49.719
You failed college twice.

18:49.787 --> 18:51.926
Which isn't nearly as bad
as your failure as a father.

18:51.994 --> 18:53.497
How's that son of yours
you never see?

18:53.565 --> 18:55.469
But you know what?
I could forgive all of that,

18:55.536 --> 18:58.444
All of it,
if you weren't such a bore.

18:58.512 --> 19:00.049
That's the worst of it, brian.

19:00.116 --> 19:03.693
You're just a big, sad,
alcoholic bore.

19:03.760 --> 19:05.263
(exhales)

19:05.331 --> 19:06.701
Well, see ya, brian.

19:06.768 --> 19:08.338
Thanks for the
(bleep) steak.

19:12.383 --> 19:13.953
Boy, it sure is nice

19:14.021 --> 19:15.658
Having our house
to ourselves again, huh?

19:15.726 --> 19:17.731
Lois?

19:17.798 --> 19:21.173
Peter, sometimes you just make
me sick to my stomach.

19:21.242 --> 19:23.647
Look, I know you
think jerome was
a good guy, but...

19:23.716 --> 19:25.453
<i>No, he was
a good guy, peter.</i>

19:25.521 --> 19:26.956
And I'm gonna
prove it to you.

19:27.024 --> 19:29.797
And you're gonna feel
like a real jackass.

19:29.865 --> 19:31.236
What's that?

19:31.303 --> 19:33.240
It's a gift.
For you.

19:33.308 --> 19:35.079
You don't deserve it,
but if anything,

19:35.147 --> 19:36.582
It's gonna wake you up
a little bit.

19:36.651 --> 19:38.388
Jerome got you this
as a thank you

19:38.456 --> 19:40.929
For letting him stay here.

19:40.997 --> 19:43.770
<i>It's an actual prop
from family ties.</i>

19:43.838 --> 19:47.480
This is... This is one
of nick's garbage sculptures.

19:47.549 --> 19:49.620
Yeah. Pretty thoughtful,
isn't it?

19:49.688 --> 19:52.729
Oh, boy, do I feel like
a jackass.

19:52.796 --> 19:55.168
Lois, I'm sorry.
I'm just...

19:55.236 --> 19:57.373
I let my jealousy
get the best of me.

19:57.441 --> 19:59.346
Jerome's such
a cool guy and I,

19:59.415 --> 20:00.851
I guess I was worried
he was cool enough

20:00.918 --> 20:02.321
To steal you away from me.

20:02.388 --> 20:04.528
You should know better
than that, peter.

20:04.597 --> 20:06.600
Now, I think you have
an apology to make.

20:16.830 --> 20:19.837
Hey, you look like
you could use a pal.

20:19.905 --> 20:21.876
Oh. Hi, peter.

20:21.944 --> 20:24.817
Look, I'm sorry
about how I acted.

20:24.884 --> 20:26.521
It's just...

20:26.589 --> 20:27.592
Lois means
everything to me.

20:27.660 --> 20:29.029
And when I saw
you together,

20:29.096 --> 20:30.700
I-- I didn't know what
was gonna happen.

20:30.768 --> 20:33.007
I just thought you might
try to mount her

20:33.075 --> 20:34.612
Or whatever it is
you guys do.

20:34.680 --> 20:37.085
Peter, how could you
even think that?

20:37.154 --> 20:39.391
I would never do
anything like that to you.

20:39.459 --> 20:41.364
You were my boy.
We were like family.

20:41.432 --> 20:43.268
Yeah, I know.

20:43.336 --> 20:44.539
I messed up bad.

20:44.607 --> 20:45.910
I'm really sorry, jerome.

20:48.651 --> 20:50.957
We cool, peter. We cool.

20:51.025 --> 20:53.866
But, listen, there is
something I got to fess up to.

20:53.934 --> 20:55.703
While I was living
with y'all,

20:55.771 --> 20:58.812
I had myself lots of
nasty ass sex with meg.

20:58.880 --> 21:00.584
I don't care about that.

21:05.134 --> 21:06.905
Hey, brian, how'd it go?

21:06.972 --> 21:08.142
Fine.

21:08.209 --> 21:09.446
Wha-- have you been crying?

21:09.513 --> 21:10.849
What happened?

21:10.918 --> 21:12.955
It didn't work.
He still hates me.

21:13.024 --> 21:14.359
You want to know something?

21:14.427 --> 21:15.629
That's okay.

21:15.697 --> 21:17.367
You don't need quagmire
to like you.

21:17.434 --> 21:21.446
You only need one person to like
you and that person is you.

21:21.514 --> 21:24.119
And I'll tell you something
else, I like you.

21:24.186 --> 21:25.323
Thanks.

21:25.390 --> 21:26.894
You want to sleep
in my room?

21:26.962 --> 21:27.930
Yeah, that'd be nice.

21:27.931 --> 22:28.931
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru